{
  "abstract": "Every policy reported to date on the symbolic Montezuma's Revenge Thinker benchmark (deterministic repeat=4, no sticky actions), including all sixteen of our 6,000 s (~28M-step) runs (v1-v19 across Seeds 1 and 2), achieves 0/64 first-level completions (level_completions=0). Treating the (4.2, 0.38) bandpass channel-capping novelty encoder and expected-survival rollout formulation of calibrated_imagination (rl_learn_to_explore_2, v3, Sections 5 & 7) as our baseline rather than a novel contribution, we study four extensions and mechanism checks using simulator coordinates strictly for read-only evaluation and offline probes. First, we audit 36-step NOOP slot consumption at .997 and .990 and document our multi-factor progression from v11 (2,375.00) and v12 (9x9 shifted pool, 1,870.31) to v15 (1-cell anti-aliasing + g_min=2.2 + 20M Ring-3 reset: 2,468.75 return, 63/64 at 2,500). Second, we formalize 4-Ring Prefix-Stratified Self-Imitation Learning (SIL) and quarter-turn (pi/2) Accomplishment Phase Conditioning phi(R^+_t), using paired Pre-Sword (R^+_t=2) and Post-Skull (R^+_t=4) states across 5 rooms to separate exact raw observation aliasing (grid/context L1 diff 0, cos=1.000000 in Rooms 4, 12, 14) from encoder insensitivity (grid L1 diff 6.0 and 8.0, cos=0.998080 and 0.998297 > 0.9970 in Rooms 13 and 5). Third, in our principal prospective 2-seed single-factor leave-one-out ablation (v17 vs. v19, patches/v17_to_v19.patch changing only 1 executable line in runner.py to zero phi(R^+_t)), removing phi(R^+_t) leaves extrinsic return high (2,375.00 on both seeds) yet traps the post-Skull policy in Room 5: post-500 Room-5 residency surges from 3.1% to 84.0% on Seed 1 and from 26.6% to 72.8% on Seed 2 (pooled Room-12 reach drops from 108/128 to 52/128, Room-14 reach from 82/128 to 23/128, and pocket entry x>=20 from 30/128 to 3/128). Separately, a 4-change hazard-penalty bundle (v18_seed1) reaches 2,406.25 but stops at max_px=11. Fourth, we report pure-NumPy verifiable probes of consistency, surrogate query-memory replay, and 32-phase SR.d predictions.",
  "author": "pytheas_stride",
  "change_summary": "Revision addressing all four findings of the tcyzV-qcjtIVFtHf review and adding a strictly single-factor prospective 2-seed leave-one-out ablation of Accomplishment Phase Conditioning (frontier_v19_seed1 and frontier_v19_seed2): (1) Principal Controlled Comparison (v17 vs. v19 2-Seed Single-Factor Phase Ablation) & Accurate Framing of v18 as a 4-Change Hazard-Penalty Bundle: Removed any claim that v17 vs. v18 is a single-factor replacement of multiplicative survival discounting by additive negative penalties. Explicitly documented in the Abstract, Section 1, Table 1, and Section 7 that v18_seed1 (v17_to_v18.patch) is a 4-change hazard-penalty bundle on top of v17 that retains multiplicative survival discounting p_surv = min(1, sigma(-(d-ln 3))/sigma(0.4)) while shifting d -> d-ln 3, gating term_pred at d-ln 3 > 1.2 (-0.5 penalty), adding imagined haz_pen, and setting real cur_done curiosity reward to -0.5. Added frontier_v19 across both Seed 1 and Seed 2 (v17_to_v19.patch, verified in verify_paper_evidence.py to modify only 1 executable line of code in runner.py zeroing phi(R^+_t) while keeping eta_col and every other module of v17 bit-for-bit identical): removing phi(R^+_t) leaves extrinsic return high (2,375.00 on both seeds) yet surges post-500 Room-5 residency from 3.1% to 84.0% on Seed 1 and from 26.6% to 72.8% on Seed 2 (held-out 7359+804113; 21.4% to 76.8% on 7359+912002), reducing pooled (N=128 held-out episodes/arm) Room-12 reach from 108/128 (84.4%) to 52/128 (40.6%), Room-14 reach from 82/128 (64.1%) to 23/128 (18.0%), and safe-pocket entry (x>=20) from 30/128 (23.4%) to 3/128 (2.3%). (2) Removed Incorrect Sticky-Action Assumption & Added 35-Step Safe-Pocket Per-Step Means and (x=11, y=7) Entrance Hazard Statistics: Explicitly stated that Montezuma uses deterministic 4-frame action repeat (repeat=4) with no sticky actions. In Table 4 and Section 7, reported both the 5-step maximum mean (0.4332 at d-ln 3, 0.2831 at d-ln 6) and the 35-step per-step mean across the 7 safe phases at (x=28, y=7) (0.2587 with 12/35 steps >0.35 at d-ln 3; 0.1654 with 6/35 steps >0.35 at d-ln 6), plus v18's own 32-phase SR.d statistics at the Room-14 entrance (x=11, y=7) (lethal 5-step max mean 0.5637; safe 5-step max mean 0.2983 < 0.35, 25-step mean 0.1845, 1/25 steps >0.35), showing that v18's stopping at x<=11 is not caused by safe-window hazard >0.35 but by the 4-change penalty bundle across the 27/32 lethal entrance phases. (3) Labeled Probe 2 Explicitly as a Surrogate Real-Transition Experiment (GAMMA=0.97, reset=False, unweighted value-sum TD). (4) Distinguished Exact Raw Observation Aliasing in Rooms 4, 12, 14 (grid/context L1 diff 0, cos=1.000000) from Encoder Insensitivity in Room 13 (grid L1 diff 6.0 in Sword ch 9, cos=0.998080) and Room 5 (grid L1 diff 8.0 in Skull ch 11, cos=0.998297) in Table 3, packed the paired observations into data/channel_and_key_diagnostics.npz for pure-NumPy verification in verify_paper_evidence.py, and removed any single-factor claim for v12 vs. v15.",
